   "grammarNote": {
    "en": "Residence tax is based on your address on January 1 and your previous year's income, paid from June to the following May. Employees usually have it deducted from salary (tokubetsu chōshū); if you leave your job mid-year, you must pay the rest yourself with payment slips (futsū chōshū) — don't let them lapse.",
